  "notes": "Official NETGEAR datasheet covers 4 models (GC728X/GC728XP/GC752X/GC752XP); data here is filtered to GC752XP. GC752XP = \"52-Port Gigabit Ethernet PoE+ Smart Cloud Switch w/2 SFP and 2 SFP+ 10G Fiber Ports\" (the \"52 ports\" = 48x RJ45 + 2x SFP + 2x SFP+). All 48 RJ45 copper ports are PoE/PoE+ (802.3af/at) capable, sharing a 505W total PoE budget (no fixed per-port note repeated below, see port 1). Rackmount (included kit) or desktop (rubber feet included); 1U, 440x320x44mm. AC input is an internal PSU (100-240VAC~50-60Hz, 10A max) with a separate, localized IEC-style AC power cord in the box, so connector is graded \"iec\" (exact C13/14 vs C19 not explicitly stated in the datasheet, but standard IEC C13/C14 is typical for this switch class/wattage). USB-A port and Micro-USB debug port have no stated speed/version in the datasheet, so no grade was set for either (Micro-USB is explicitly \"for debugging only,\" not general data transfer). SFP/SFP+ cages are unpopulated (transceivers sold separately); connector modeled as generic \"sfp\" per catalog convention, with grade reflecting max supported line rate (SFP = dedicated 1G/100M, 1000BASE-X; SFP+ = dedicated 10G/1G, 10GBASE-X).",
